Implementation:
1. `internal/db/effective.go`
   - Introduced `membershipResolver` with model, aggregate dependency `reads`, and a map of completed group results.
   - Moved recursive `resolve` and `selectRule` onto it.
   - Target, within and descendant expansion all use the same resolver.
   - `effectiveOf` creates a resolver per calculation.
   - Shared results are copied into selector sets before narrowing, so cached membership maps are not modified.
   - Dependency reads remain aggregated across the entire traversal; existing model cache invalidation stays intact.
2. `internal/db/draft.go`
   - `draftMembers` creates one resolver and shares it across draft rules, covering previews and description paths.
3. `internal/db/rulework_security_test.go`
   - `repeatedRuleGroups` creates the graph through ordinary member API writes.
   - `TestRepeatedGroupRulesDoNotMultiplyMembershipWork` is the allocation-growth regression; it failed before the fix.
   - `TestMembersCanQueryRepeatedGroupRules` queries through the ordinary API and checks direct rule reasons, then removes/adds base memberships and verifies outer membership updates.

No new permission policy, input limit, refusal, flag, fallback, production test hook, schema change or dependency was introduced. Cost/tradeoff: temporary result maps for the duration of one membership calculation.

